<BaseLayout title="About — Quiet Compass" description="The point of view behind Quiet Compass: practical decisions, visible reasoning, and honest evidence." route="C03"><section><div class="shell"><span class="route">About / A point of view</span><h1>Useful first.<br/><em>Character always.</em></h1><div class="case-grid"><div class="prose"><p class="lead">Quiet Compass is an independent digital-design portfolio exploring how complicated experiences can become easier to understand.</p><h2>Design should help someone do something.</h2><p>A beautiful interface can still leave someone wondering what happens next. The work here starts with that moment: the decision a person is trying to make, the context they need, and the confidence to continue.</p><p>That is why the projects show both the starting point and the chosen direction. The alternative matters. The tradeoff matters. A screen without that reasoning only tells half the story.</p><h2>Small decisions, explained.</h2><p>Atlas explores workflow structure. Fieldnote connects specialist expertise to a clearer editorial identity. Threshold examines the first useful moment in onboarding. Each is an original concept study, with assumptions and untested outcomes identified rather than dressed up as research.</p><h2>How a collaboration should feel.</h2><p>A focused brief. Tangible work early enough to question it. Decisions recorded in language everyone can use. A handoff that describes what works, what remains uncertain, and what should happen next. These are the principles behind the practice—not claims about an undisclosed client list.</p><h2>What this portfolio does not claim.</h2><p>The concept work is not commissioned client work. No client identities, testimonials, or commercial performance results have been invented. The site makes its evidence boundaries visible so the work can be judged on what is actually here.</p><a class="btn" href={withBase('work/')}>Inspect the work →</a></div><aside class="panel case-aside"><span class="route">The working principles</span><h2 style="font-size:2rem">A calmer way through.</h2><p><strong>Make the next step legible.</strong><br/>People should not need a tour of the interface before using it.</p><p><strong>Show the tradeoff.</strong><br/>A choice is stronger when its cost is understood.</p><p><strong>Keep the person in control.</strong><br/>Motion, navigation, and recovery should support agency.</p><p><strong>Be precise about evidence.</strong><br/>A concept is a proposal. A test is a test. A measured result needs a source.</p><a class="text-link" href={withBase('colophon/')}>How this site is made →</a></aside></div></div></section></BaseLayout>
